Title: I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT A SPEC WAS
Author: vibecode-blog pipeline
Contact: @lazy_genius2025

== act: hook ==

INT. COZY REMOTE CABIN - DAY

A CLAY CHARACTER sits by a fireplace with a single laptop. Out the window, three distant DESKTOP TOWERS are visible in a snowy city, glowing with a synchronized blue light.

NARRATOR
(cool, nonchalant)
My three computers finally act like one. I can work from anywhere.

The character clicks a button. The blue light pulses across all three distant machines simultaneously.

NARRATOR
(cynical)
But getting here? It took six months of absolute, unadulterated hell.

== act: fury ==

INT. DARK MESSY OFFICE - NIGHT

The character is buried under a mountain of tangled, pulsating red clay wires. A monitor flashes "CRITICAL FAILURE" in a harsh red strobe.

NARRATOR
(pissed)
Monday morning. Everything stopped. Ten thousand lines of code, and half of it was pure garbage.

CLOSE UP - MONITOR

A jagged crack opens in the center of the screen. A door handle emerges, labeled "SHELL INJECTION".

NARRATOR
(raw)
AI wrote a back door. I approved it. I didn't even know it was there.

== act: mess ==

INT. THE CODE JUNGLE - DAY

The character hacks through a forest of rapidly duplicating clay vines with a rusty machete. Five identical STUBBY ROBOTS are building five different, conflicting wooden bridges over the same stream.

NARRATOR
(manic)
Five agents building the same thing. Three date formatters. Four ways to validate a string.

The character grabs a vine, and the entire forest warps into a giant, suffocating knot of clay.

NARRATOR
(cynical)
It looked convincing. That's why it was dangerous. I was vibe coding with no map.

== act: insight ==

INT. CLEAN OFF-WHITE STUDIO - DAY

The character pins a simple, 4-line blueprint to a pristine wall. The lines are sharp and minimal.

NARRATOR
(resolute)
Implementation is free. But deciding what to build? That's the only thing that isn't.

WIDE SHOT

The character walks across a sturdy, simple clay bridge. The messy jungle is replaced by a vast, organized grid.

NARRATOR
(philosopher)
Specs don't come from conference rooms. They come from the grind.
